# gitleaks fingerprint ignore file for the backend.
#
# Picked up automatically: `gitleaks detect`'s `-i/--gitleaks-ignore-path` defaults to `.`, the
# current working directory, and `backend/scripts/ci.ps1` does `Push-Location $backendRoot` before
# running the secret-scan gate — so this file must live at `backend/.gitleaksignore`, not the repo
# root. A root-level file is read by nothing and the gate stays red while looking unfixed.
#
# IMPORTANT — these fingerprints are only immutable because the scan runs in GIT MODE (no
# `--no-git`). A git-mode fingerprint is `<commit>:<file>:<rule>:<line>`, anchored to immutable
# commit content, so an entry can never drift onto different content or mask a finding it was not
# written for. If the scan mode ever changes — `--no-git`, or gitleaks' newer `dir` command — the
# commit segment disappears and a fingerprint degrades to `<file>:<rule>:<line>` against MUTABLE
# working-tree content, at which point an entry here could silently suppress an unrelated real
# secret that later lands at the same path/rule/line. TASK-0016 is expected to rewrite these gate
# scripts: whoever does that MUST re-derive every fingerprint below against the new mode rather
# than carrying this file forward unchanged.
#
